---
description: Rails 8 conventions for the sample todo app
alwaysApply: true
---

- Prefer Turbo Streams over custom JavaScript for partial page updates
- Keep all migrations reversible (define both `up`/`down` or use `change` with reversible methods)
- Use `params.expect()` for strong parameters, not the older `params.require().permit()` pattern
- Use `bin/rails generate` rather than hand-writing boilerplate controllers, models, or migrations
- Keep the schema scoped to the todo app — do not import or reference models/migrations from other projects
- Place shared view partials in `app/views/todos/` with a `_` prefix
- Turbo Stream view files follow the naming convention `action.turbo_stream.erb` inside the relevant views folder
